Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: advertise color management only when all mixers have DSPP

The SC7280 DPU used by the SM-T733 has three layer mixers, but only LM_0
has a DSPP. DPU exposes CTM and gamma LUT on every CRTC as soon as the
catalog contains any DSPP. A compositor can then set a gamma LUT on the
external DP CRTC. At 1920x1080 it needs the LM_2/LM_3 pair, neither of
which has a DSPP, so atomic resource reservation fails with -ENAVAIL and
the monitor goes black after detection.

The advertised CRTC color properties cannot be tied to a particular
mixer: resource allocation can place any CRTC on any mixer. Only expose
them when every mixer has a DSPP, so userspace does not submit a color
configuration that some display pipelines cannot satisfy.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1911,7 +1911,12 @@ struct drm_crtc *dpu_crtc_init(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_plane *plane,
 
 	drm_crtc_helper_add(crtc, &dpu_crtc_helper_funcs);
 
-	if (dpu_kms->catalog->dspp_count) {
+	/* A CRTC can use any mixer. Do not advertise color properties when
+	 * some mixers have no DSPP: userspace may otherwise request a LUT on
+	 * a pipeline that cannot reserve the required color processing block.
+	 */
+	if (dpu_kms->catalog->dspp_count &&
+	    dpu_kms->catalog->dspp_count == dpu_kms->catalog->mixer_count) {
 		const struct dpu_dspp_cfg *dspp = &dpu_kms->catalog->dspp[0];
 
 		if (dspp->sblk->gc.base) {
